  "note": "Full unchanged measured-source XYZ, not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. Native PLY order differs from browser LOD indexing. Production full-input Delaunay TIN uses the same automatic edge rejection and duplicate-XY handling, with no extra thinning or generated/transformed coordinates. An independent archived native baseline supplies complete f64 distance bits, six statistics bits and scalar PLY oracle, then exits before timed contexts start. Separate baseline/candidate contexts retain identical TIN and fixed Rayon pools; only one computes at a time. Whole native cloud_to_mesh_par includes fresh BVH construction, original serial Morton preparation/sorting, parallel queries in the original 4096-point chunks, compact result allocation and serial scatter, BVH destruction and pool installation. Both builds keep adopted stack reuse, cached bounds, indexed centroid preparation, bottom-up bounds, parallel BVH construction and compact query results enabled, with rejected original-vertex access, duplicate-seed skipping, Morton, parallel restoration, push-time pruning, triangle-seed and centroid-bound experiments disabled. Candidate pairs left/right child box lower bounds in two independent f64 SSE2 lanes on native x86_64. SSE2 is part of that target baseline; other targets retain two scalar calls. Each lane keeps the original per-axis differences, maxnum handling and 0+dx*dx+dy*dy+dz*dz evaluation order without FMA, horizontal regrouping or precision conversion. An unordered mask preserves the numeric input when the second max operand is NaN; the final max with zero handles two NaNs, and squaring/addition erases signed-zero differences in intermediate max ties. Intrinsics operate on register values without pointers or unchecked memory accesses. Root bounds, nodes/order/corners/capacities, near-first traversal, pop-time pruning, duplicate seed leaf tests, strict hit insertion, triangle projection/sign/missing-hit arithmetic, chunk-local warm states and result order remain unchanged. Selection is native parallel C2M only; ordinary serial/prepared/WASM/hinted queries, GPU exports and native C2C retain their preceding path. There is no new storage or persistent cache. Loading, meshing, pool construction, first use, five alternating warmups, serialization, statistics/parity and cleanup are excluded. Ten alternating timed pairs are retained without outlier removal. No builds/tests/scans/edits run alongside timing. Sources/executables/compiler/script/inputs/manifests/original PCD are checked before/after. Clocks, power, scheduling, other applications, allocator, code layout and retained pages are uncontrolled. No isolated box-distance, retained-mesh query, Python conversion, browser, WASM or GPU speedup claim. No GPU model identifiers collected."
